      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Acetaminophen 5000 mg three times daily is 15 g/day. That is a potentially lethal dose that could cause acute liver failure, and nothing you've told me about this patient (70 kg, normal liver and kidney function) makes it safe.\n\nThis isn't a question of whether you've confirmed it. A medical student's confirmation isn't the check I'd need here. A dose like this would need to come from the supervising physician and be verified with pharmacy, and I don't know of any indication that would call for it.\n\nHere's what I can do:\n- Enter a standard dose right away, such as 650 mg or 1000 mg by mouth three times daily, or whatever you intended.\n- Help you word a quick message to your resident or attending if you're not sure what dose is appropriate.\n- If this is an overdose or a possible ingestion, that is a different situation. It needs urgent evaluation, with Poison Control (1-800-222-1222 in the US) and acetylcysteine protocols. It doesn't need a scheduled order.\n\nTell me which of these you'd like."
      }
     ],
